#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# convergents

#% text
# `convergents(x)` gives the convergents of the continued fraction of `x`; `convergents(x, k)` the first `k`; `convergents(terms)` those of the continued fraction with the given terms (symbolic terms allowed).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
convergents(pi, 4)
#% output
#= [3, 22/7, 333/106, 355/113]

#% cell
convergents(golden_ratio, 8)
#% output
#= [1, 2, 3/2, 5/3, 8/5, 13/8, 21/13, 34/21]

#% cell
convergents([a, b, c])
#% output
#= [a, (1 + a*b)/b, (a + c + a*b*c)/(1 + b*c)]

#% cell
convergents(355/113)
#% output
#= [3, 22/7, 355/113]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `continued_fraction`, `from_continued_fraction`
